<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<section xml:id="ch-maps" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Mathematics major map</title>

  <p>
    The major from the 2026<ndash/>27 Bulletin on one page: lower division, the
    seven upper-division courses by category, the five emphases, and the minor.
    Each box is a course and each arrow runs from a prerequisite to the course
    that needs it. Gold arrows feed a course offered only in alternate years,
    which is where timing goes wrong most often. Hover over a course to light up
    what it needs and what it unlocks; hover over an emphasis to see the courses
    it requires.
    <url href="external/major-map.html" visual="">Open full size</url>
    or <url href="external/major-map.pdf" visual="">download as PDF</url>.
  </p>
  <interactive xml:id="major-map" iframe="major-map.html" width="100%" aspect="1920:1240">
    <static><p>Interactive map of the mathematics major (available in the HTML version).</p></static>
  </interactive>

</section>
